.TH MFCJ5720DW-MONITOR 1 "November 2026" "mfcj5720dw-cups 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mfcj5720dw-monitor \- monitor a Brother MFC-J5720DW network printer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mfcj5720dw-monitor
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Display physical printer status, diagnostic messages, four ink levels and
recent jobs belonging to the current user in a local CUPS queue.
Poll the printer and CUPS every five seconds without blocking the window.
The Maintenance window submits head-cleaning and nozzle-check jobs through
the selected local CUPS queue. Ink-level synchronization runs automatically
when needed.
Optional scan-to-PC reception registers temporary destinations with SNMP writes
and acquires documents through Brother's separately installed brscan4 SANE backend.
.PP
Desktop notifications report new faults, recovery, a paused queue and
observed job delivery, cancellation or failure.
Two consecutive failed polls trigger a connectivity notification.
An unavailable measurement is displayed as unavailable, never as zero ink.
The initial job list does not generate notifications for old completed jobs.
.PP
The monitor can remain running when its window is closed. A system tray icon
remains visible while it runs, including when started with --background.
Activate the icon or choose Show monitor from its menu to reopen the window.
Use Quit monitor in the window or tray menu to stop it and remove the icon.
Login startup is an explicit preference.
Use Apply to save preferences and the selected printer.
.PP
The desktop must provide a StatusNotifierItem host. GNOME requires the
AppIndicator and KStatusNotifierItem Support extension (Fedora package
gnome-shell-extension-appindicator). Enable appindicatorsupport@rgcjonas.gmail.com
with gnome-extensions; a newly installed extension may require logging out and
back in first. Its single click opens the menu; a double-click opens the window.
Without a tray host, launch the application again to reopen its existing window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-queue " " \fIQUEUE\fR
Follow this local CUPS queue. Otherwise use the saved selection or the first
MFC-J5720DW queue. CUPS is contacted through its local Unix socket.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-host " " \fIHOST\fR
Query this bare host name, IPv4 or IPv6 address.
Do not include a URI scheme, brackets or a port.
Without an override, derive the address from a socket, LPD, IPP or IPPS queue.
For a DNS-SD service URI, USB queue or print-server URI, enter the physical
printer's address explicitly. The printer must be reachable over the network.
.TP
.BR \-\-community " " \fICOMMUNITY\fR
SNMP read community (default: public). SNMPv2c queries use UDP port 161.
The community is saved in a private user settings file when Apply is used.
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start monitoring without showing the window.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Print a single textual status report and exit. No graphical session is needed.
Exit status is 0 on an SNMP reply, 1 when unavailable, or 2 for invalid options.
A successful query can still report a printer fault or unsupported diagnostics.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.SH MAINTENANCE
Click Maintenance to open a separate window to clean all print heads, black only or colors only,
using normal, strong or strongest cleaning. Clean print heads shows the
selected queue, intensity and ink group before confirmation. Stronger
cleaning consumes more ink. Cancel is the default confirmation button.
.PP
Print nozzle check prints one internal print-quality sheet.
Status, ink bars and CUPS jobs refresh automatically every five seconds.
If CUPS supply levels differ from the printer's readings or are unavailable,
the monitor submits a paperless ReportLevels job. The queue must be idle,
accept jobs and support the command. The monitored address must match the
address derived from the queue, and printer ink readings must be valid.
Attempts are separated by at least five minutes, including after failure.
Only one ink update is tracked at a time. Matching levels create no jobs.
Automatic supply queries do not generate document-delivery notifications.
One last-update time covers the displayed printer information, including ink
levels. Ink synchronization shows a temporary progress message, cleared on
confirmed completion, or an error if the job fails, is cancelled or cannot be
confirmed. The job is queried directly, independently of the bounded job history.
.PP
Select a local CUPS queue under Printer and notifications and press Apply.
An IP address alone is insufficient. Commands use the selected queue's device,
including when the address used for status monitoring has been overridden.
Only advertised commands are enabled, and the queue must accept jobs.
Capabilities are rechecked before submission. Use the Brother MFC-J5720DW CUPS
driver to expose all operations.
.PP
Each action submits one application/vnd.cups-command job with one copy.
Queue defaults are preserved. Cleaning and nozzle-check job IDs are displayed; acceptance or delivery
does not prove physical maintenance completion. A paused queue retains jobs
until resumed. Check the job list before retrying an unconfirmed submission.
Closing the maintenance window keeps the monitor running and retains the
cleaning selections. Hiding the main window also hides maintenance.
Quitting dismisses an open confirmation or waits for an in-flight submission;
it does not cancel accepted jobs or wait for physical maintenance completion.
Use the printer's own maintenance menu for alignment.
.SH SCAN TO PC
Install Brother's 64-bit brscan4 scanner backend and configure this model with
brsaneconfig4, using a unique scanner name and the printer's literal IPv4
address (ip=, not nodename=). The monitor matches this configuration to SANE's
device list. It does not require the separate brscan-skey program.
.PP
Expand Scan to this PC, enable reception and set the PC name, output folder,
resolution and OCR languages. Press Apply, then choose this PC from
the printer's File, Image, OCR or Email menu.
Click the output folder to open the GTK folder chooser. Select a folder, then
press Apply to save it. Cancelling the chooser keeps the previous folder.
The proposed PC name combines the system hostname and login name, separated by
" de " (for example "quad de laurent"). The complete string is truncated to its
first 15 characters; unsupported characters become underscores. Saved names are
preserved. Clear the name and press Apply to restore, display and save the
default; a name containing only spaces has the same effect. Other settings
are preserved. Custom names may also contain spaces and dots.
.PP
Available resolutions are 100, 150, 200, 300, 400, 600, 1200 and 2400 dpi;
the default is 300 dpi. Optical resolution depends on the physical input.
.PP
File saves a multipage PDF. Image saves JPEG pages and opens the first image.
OCR uses Tesseract to save only a searchable PDF, then opens the PDF.
Email opens the default mail composer with a PDF attachment; it never sends
email automatically. Final documents and scan.log remain in a new private
subdirectory for each job. All PNG working images are deleted after success,
failure or cancellation. Image output uses JPEG quality 95. Quitting waits
for acquisition cleanup to finish.
.PP
Choose Off, Long edge or Short edge in the printer's duplex menu. The monitor
reads that choice before acquisition. Duplex selects the feeder; short-edge
scans rotate back pages 180 degrees before image, PDF or OCR output.
For one-sided scans, the printer automatically uses the feeder when loaded,
otherwise the glass. All available pages are acquired; a glass scan produces
one page. Old source preferences are ignored. Resolution and grayscale come
from the monitor.
An unreadable panel setting stops the job. Use Cancel scan to stop acquisition.
A job is limited to 500 pages and 20 minutes.
.PP
Allow UDP 54925 from the printer through the PC firewall. The temporary
destinations use SNMPv1 with community internal, independently of the read
community. Acquisition uses TCP 54921 via brscan4 and scanimage.
A VM behind NAT requires forwarding or a bridged network. The optional PC
address sets the advertised IPv4 address; it does not configure forwarding.
.PP
Keep the monitor running to receive scans; hiding the window is sufficient when
background monitoring is enabled. Login startup is optional. Quitting cancels
acquisition and stops registration renewals. The PC entry can remain visible
until the six-minute lease expires. Another receiver, such as brscan-skey,
cannot use UDP 54925 concurrently. Only network IPv4 scan-button events are
supported. This legacy protocol is unencrypted and unauthenticated.
.PP
Launching the monitor again in the same desktop session opens the existing
instance. Different users can each monitor printer status, but only one
instance on the PC can receive scans at a time.
.SH LIMITATIONS
CUPS completion means that the backend finished sending the job. It is not
proof that the printer has finished producing all sheets. A job disappearing
from CUPS history is not treated as successful completion.
.PP
The printer's display text and diagnostic state also reflect maintenance.
The monitor does not infer completion of a particular cleaning operation from
an idle state and does not offer an alignment wizard.
Unknown Brother status codes remain visible with the printer's own message.
Alerts and job history are bounded to 16 and 20 entries per query respectively.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mfcj5720dw-monitor/settings.ini
.br
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/io.github.vivier.mfcj5720dw.monitor.desktop
.PP
XDG_CONFIG_HOME defaults to ~/.config.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mfcj5720dw-monitor --queue Brother-MFC-J5720DW
mfcj5720dw-monitor --host 192.168.100.2 --once
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lpstat (1),
.BR scanimage (1),
.BR tesseract (1),
.BR commandtomfcj5720dw (1)
